  "policies": {
    "operating_leases": "Rent remains in operating expense; do not subtract operating lease liabilities or add operating ROU assets to EV.",
    "finance_leases": "Consolidated D&A including finance ROU amortization is added back; modeled new finance ROU asset additions are economic capex. Finance debt must be explicitly supplied in allocation; June split is unknown. Do not subtract finance lease principal in FCFF again.",
    "affiliate_interests": "All equity earnings excluded from operating forecasts. Affiliate royalties remain operating revenue. Ownership stakes valued separately only under explicit allocation policy; no dividends or equity income included in core FCFF.",
    "sbc": "Full economic SBC stays in SGA as cash replacement. No SBC addback, mechanical future share dilution, or buyback-funded EPS uplift. Additional award reserve must cover only incremental existing claims not already charged via future compensation.",
    "next": "Rent relief reduces rent revenue and EBIT exactly once. Capital support appears in cash capex exactly once. Remaining 2031\u201336 support is explicit. The 2037 terminal year removes the finite support but requires g/ROIC economic reinvestment.",
    "terminal": "Terminal NOPAT = normalized 2036 EBIT without NEXT relief \u00d7 (1+g) \u00d7 (1-tax). FCFF = terminal NOPAT \u00d7 (1-g/ROIC). No second capex/D&A/NWC deduction in terminal. Ongoing $50\u2013100m restructuring-like expense persists through terminal.",
    "tax": "Normalized cash-tax proxy, not a forecast of each jurisdiction or a reuse of one-off discrete H1 tax benefits. No separate deferred-tax asset added.",
    "cashflow_timing": "Remaining H2 2026 is valued at 0.5 years; 2027\u20132036 at 1.5\u201310.5 years (year-end convention). H2 EBIT/DA/cash-capex deduct observed H1. H2 finance additions and NWC are explicitly estimated; no fictitious observed H1 finance capex.",
    "capex": "Forecast full investment in corporate real estate/equipment plus economic finance-lease assets. Excludes franchisees own capex; no systemwide restaurant assets added to bridge.",
    "units": "Store-count growth is a separate illustration, not multiplied into sales after the explicit unit-sales contribution. Sales use comp \u00d7 unit contribution \u00d7 FX."
